From: rams95 <rams95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:58:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0021-native-option-rows-host-calls.patch

PC settings as real rows of the game's own Options list (title and in-game menu): Resolution, Anti-aliasing, Cutscene
bars, Lens rain, Mouse look, between Sound and Screen color/brightness ('Adjust screen position' left out). The game's
list engine draws them, moves its cursor over them, handles Left/Right and shows their help line: the host builds a new
row table in memory the game does not use (0x80000), points the list at it, and the rows' get/set functions are host
functions the game calls (ps2::register_host_call: guest addresses 0x0FF00000+ run host code). Their words are pictures
in the game's own label sheet (texture override from tools/rd_options.py, sprites reached through the RAM mirror).
PS2_NATIVE_OPTIONS=1, PS2_NATIVE_OPTIONS_ART=options_art.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
